Prefix every Bash command with `chop`.

**Why:** Noisy output (git, tsc, docker, npm) wastes context window tokens. CHOP compresses output and improves efficiency.

**How to apply:** `chop git status`, `chop git log`, `chop node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit`, etc. Commands that produce only a few lines may skip `chop`, but default to using it when in doubt.
